"program_narrative": "Program DB2HNDL is a batch DB2 template program that demonstrates standard embedded-SQL operations against the PORTFOLIO table. It clears its host variables and null indicators, connects to database 'sample', then runs example operations in fixed order: insert portfolio 'PORT00001' named 'TEST PORTFOLIO' with the current date and timestamp, total value 0 and status 'A'; select that portfolio's columns into host variables; open a cursor over all portfolios with status 'A' and fetch rows until no more rows remain, performing 2310-PROCESS-CURSOR-ROW for each row fetched (that paragraph is not present in the source, so per-row processing is unknown); set the portfolio's status to 'I'; and delete it. Each operation except the cursor is followed by a common SQL check that displays the SQLCODE and error text on any non-zero SQLCODE and, for a negative SQLCODE, rolls back, sets return code 8, commits and disconnects, and ends the program. On normal completion the program commits the work and resets the connection.",
